---
/**
 * `Vybavení chalupy` + `Sociální zařízení` + `Přehled vybavení`   the second
 * section of /ubytovani.
 *
 * UPDATE: `Sociální zařízení` moved here from Loznice.astro, by request, so
 * that `Vybavení chalupy` sits ABOVE it. The page now reads
 *
 *   Ložnice a pokoje   (split, media-right)
 *   Vybavení chalupy   (split, media-left)
 *   Sociální zařízení  (two cards)
 *   Přehled vybavení   (five lists)
 *
 * i.e. the two prose+photograph splits run back to back and the two card
 * blocks follow. Nothing about the bathroom copy or its markup changed in the
 * move   only its parent section. It reads correctly under this heading: a
 * bathroom's fittings ARE cottage equipment, and the block keeps its own h3.
 *
 * COPY IS THE OLD SITE'S, VERBATIM: three paragraphs of prose, then the five
 * lists. Nothing is reworded and nothing is dropped. See the header of
 * src/data/vybaveni.ts for the one entry that carries a caveat and why.
 *
 * DESIGN: the split again, mirrored   media-LEFT this time, because the section
 * above is media-right and alternating sides down the page is the rule
 * (docs/02-design-system.md §3). UPDATE: the photograph is now the living room
 * (obyvak, DSC_4579-scaled-1-1.jpg), matching the first and most substantial
 * paragraph ("Obývací pokoj je vybaven krbem, stolem, koženou sedačkou a
 * velkou plochou TV..."). It used to be the covered terrace, which only the
 * third and shortest paragraph is about; Loznice.astro's split-media above
 * took a bedroom photo instead, which freed this one up for the room its own
 * copy actually opens on.
 *
 * ⚠ BAND: --omitka, by request, not --kamen. This is the one deviation from
 * docs/02-design-system.md §3's "no two adjacent bands share a ground"   the
 * section directly above (Loznice) is also --omitka. The two still read as
 * separate sections because the split mirrors sides (media-right, then
 * media-left) and each has its own photograph; nothing here relies on the
 * ground colour to mark the boundary. If that ever stops being enough, the fix
 * is a divider between them (RoofDivider, the device Vybaveni's own
 * `Přehled vybavení` half already uses), not reverting to --kamen.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THE OVERVIEW WAS FIVE COLUMNS OF PLAIN TEXT AND IT STILL IS.
 *
 * On the old page these were five headed lists floated three-across, with a
 * hanging en dash before each entry and nothing else   no rule, no ground, no
 * mark. It was hard to scan, but it was hard to scan because it was UNDESIGNED,
 * not because it was five lists. So this keeps the five lists, in the old order,
 * with the old words, and does the typographic work instead: a group icon, a
 * tick, a card ground, and columns that actually align.
 *
 * It is deliberately NOT re-sorted, NOT merged into three groups, and NOT
 * trimmed of the entries that are about the surroundings rather than the
 * cottage. Those would all be content decisions and this pass does not make
 * content decisions.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import obyvak from '@img/DSC_4579-scaled-1-1.jpg';
import IconLucide from '../../IconLucide.astro';
import RoofDivider from '../../decor/RoofDivider.astro';
import { SOCIALNI_ZARIZENI, VYBAVENI } from '../../../data/vybaveni';
---

<section id="vybaveni" class="vybaveni" aria-labelledby="vybaveni-nadpis">
  <div class="split split--media-left">
    <div class="split-media">
      {/*
        UPDATE: this was zastrwsena-veranda-krb-14e3-.jpeg, 1000 x 667   the
        "replacement shot" docs/01-content.md §10 called the most valuable
        photograph the site could be given. It has arrived (DSC_5192.webp,
        3096 x 2064, the same terrace and fireplace) and now renders here.
      */}
      <Image
        src={obyvak}
        alt="Obývací pokoj chalupy Heřmanka s krbem, koženou sedačkou a dlouhým jídelním stolem pod dřevěným trámovým stropem"
        widths={[500, 750, 1000, 1500]}
        sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 50vw, 100vw"
        width={1920}
        height={1282}
        format="webp"
        quality={68}
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="split-body">
      <div data-reveal="up">
        <h2 id="vybaveni-nadpis">Vybavení chalupy</h2>
        <p>
          Obývací pokoj je vybaven krbem, stolem, koženou sedačkou a&nbsp;velkou
          plochou TV s&nbsp;více než 100&nbsp;kanály. Kuchyně je plně vybavena
          a&nbsp;to: troubou, varnou deskou, lednicí, kávovarem, rychlovarnou
          konvicí, myčkou na nádobí a&nbsp;mikrovlnnou troubou (příbory
          a&nbsp;talíře, sklenice jsou samozřejmostí). V&nbsp;objektu je
          k&nbsp;dispozici i&nbsp;pračka a&nbsp;sušička.
        </p>
        <p>
          Ložnice jsou vybaveny postelemi s&nbsp;pohodlnými novými matracemi
          a&nbsp;skříněmi.
        </p>
        <p>
          Terasa (spodní) disponuje venkovním krbem a&nbsp;posezením. Horní terasa
          disponuje posezením.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/*
    The bathrooms sit under the split rather than inside it. They are a
    comparison   the same three things on two floors   and a comparison wants
    two columns side by side, not a sentence that makes the reader hold one
    floor in their head while they read the other.
  */}
  <div class="wrap zarizeni">
    <RoofDivider class="zarizeni-divider" />

    <h3 id="zarizeni-nadpis" data-reveal="up">Sociální zařízení</h3>

    {/*
      The shower/bath icon is the one real difference between the floors
      the copy says a shower on 1. NP and a tub on 2. NP   so it is what tells
      the two cards apart at a glance, rather than a repeated generic mark.
    */}
    <ul class="zarizeni-grid" role="list" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="80">
      {
        SOCIALNI_ZARIZENI.map((z, i) => (
          <li class="card zarizeni-karta">
            <p class="zarizeni-patro">
              <IconLucide
                name={i === 0 ? 'shower-head' : 'bath'}
                size={18}
                class="zarizeni-ikona"
              />
              <span>{i === 0 ? '1. NP' : '2. NP'}</span>
            </p>
            <ul role="list">
              {z.polozky.map((p) => <li>{p}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prehled">
    <RoofDivider class="prehled-divider" />

    <h3 id="prehled-nadpis" data-reveal="up">Přehled vybavení</h3>

    <div class="prehled-grid" data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="80">
      {
        VYBAVENI.map((skupina) => (
          <section class="skupina" aria-labelledby={`skupina-${skupina.klic}`}>
            <h4 id={`skupina-${skupina.klic}`} class="skupina-nadpis">
              <IconLucide name={skupina.icon} size={20} class="skupina-ikona" />
              <span>{skupina.nazev}</span>
            </h4>

            <ul role="list">
              {
                skupina.polozky.map((p) => (
                  <li>
                    <IconLucide
                      name={p.overit ? 'circle-alert' : 'circle-check'}
                      size={16}
                      class:list={['polozka-ikona', p.overit && 'polozka-ikona--overit']}
                    />
                    <span>
                      {p.nazev}
                      {/*
                        The caveat is rendered INSIDE the item, never as a
                        footnote and never suppressed. An entry that needs one
                        must not be able to appear as a plain tick   see the
                        argument in src/data/vybaveni.ts.
                      */}
                      {p.overit && <span class="polozka-overit">{p.overit}</span>}
                    </span>
                  </li>
                ))
              }
            </ul>
          </section>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .vybaveni {
    background-color: var(--color-omitka);
  }

  h2 {
    /* --mosaz-tmava on --omitka = 6.05:1. Plain --mosaz would be 4.30:1   the
       failure §1.2 warns about. */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  /* `p` has no margin in global.css by design   see the note in Loznice.astro. */
  .split-body p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /*
   * ---- Photo bleed, media-left only -------------------------------------
   *
   * The photograph runs taller than the text beside it and overflows the
   * row at the BOTTOM   so it reads as the bigger of the two halves
   * instead of matching the text column's height like every other split on
   * the page.
   *
   * ⚠ IT USED TO OVERFLOW THE TOP AS WELL (`inset-block: -3rem`) AND MUST NOT
   * AGAIN. The section above is now the `Ložnice a pokoje` split, whose own
   * photograph is media-RIGHT and runs to the section boundary. A top bleed
   * pushed this picture 3rem up past that boundary, so the two photographs met
   * as a staircase with this one's top edge slicing into the bottom of the
   * bedroom copy. Squared off at the boundary they meet corner to corner
   * instead   text, photo / photo, text   which is the point of alternating
   * the sides in the first place. (Before `Sociální zařízení` moved out of
   * Loznice.astro the section above ended in cards, and the top bleed had
   * nothing to collide with. It does now.)
   *
   * Desktop only, same threshold as the rest of the split
   * (docs/02-design-system.md's two-column split activates at 64rem); below
   * that the two stack and there is no row height to break out of.
   *
   * Taking the photo out of flow with `position: absolute` is what makes the
   * overflow possible: a grid item sized by `min-height` still gets clamped
   * to the row's own height, but an absolutely positioned box with `top` and
   * `bottom` both set is sized directly from its containing block, ignoring
   * the row entirely. `.split-body` needs `grid-column: 2` because it is now
   * the only item left in flow, and a lone grid item auto-places into the
   * first column, not the second.
   */
  @media (width >= 64rem) {
    .split {
      position: relative;
    }

    .split-media {
      position: absolute;
      inset-block: 0 -3rem;
      inset-inline-start: 0;
      width: 50%;
    }

    .split-body {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }

  /* ---- The two card blocks --------------------------------------------- */

  /*
   * The top padding is load-bearing. The split above runs its photograph past
   * the bottom of its own row (the bleed, three rules up), so without this the
   * `Sociální zařízení` heading starts hard against the picture and reads as a
   * caption on it rather than as a new heading.
   *
   * The two blocks take the SAME top padding, so each divider carries the same
   * air above it. `.zarizeni` has no bottom padding: it and `.prehled` are in
   * one section now, so the gap between the bathroom cards and the `Přehled
   * vybavení` divider is `.prehled`'s top padding alone, not the two sections'
   * padding stacked as it was when they lived in separate files.
   */
  .zarizeni,
  .prehled {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .zarizeni {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .prehled {
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .zarizeni,
    .prehled {
      padding-top: 4.5rem;
    }

    .prehled {
      padding-bottom: 6rem;
    }
  }

  /*
   * Equal padding is not equal SPACE above 64rem, because that is where the
   * photograph starts bleeding 3rem past the bottom of its row and eats the
   * first block's padding from the top. Add the 3rem back so both dividers
   * measure the same distance from whatever sits above them   without this the
   * first sits 104px below the photo and the second 152px below the cards, and
   * the pair reads as two different rhythms rather than one.
   */
  @media (width >= 64rem) {
    .zarizeni {
      padding-top: 7.5rem;
    }
  }

  /* The divider does the separating now, so the heading sits closer under it
     than it did under bare padding. */
  .zarizeni-divider,
  .prehled-divider {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-title-m);
    color: var(--color-les);
  }

  /* ---- Sociální zařízení ------------------------------------------------ */

  .zarizeni-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    /* Two cards of short lines do not need the full 1280   at full width the
       pair reads as two distant columns. */
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 40rem) {
    .zarizeni-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }

  .zarizeni-patro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  .zarizeni-ikona {
    flex: none;
    /* An icon is a fill, so plain brass is correct here (§1.2). */
    color: var(--color-mosaz);
  }

  .zarizeni-karta ul {
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .zarizeni-karta li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  /* An en dash, not a disc: the same marker the old site used for its lists. */
  .zarizeni-karta li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  .zarizeni-karta li::before {
    content: '–';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    /* Brass AS TEXT, so the darker step (§1.2). */
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
  }

  /* ---- Přehled vybavení ------------------------------------------------ */

  /*
   * ⚠ TWO COLUMNS, NOT THREE, AND THE REASON IS ARITHMETIC.
   *
   * The five groups are wildly uneven   5, 13, 5, 5, 8 entries. A column flow
   * balances by height while `break-inside: avoid` keeps each group whole, so
   * the count per column is what decides whether it looks deliberate.
   *
   *   two columns:   5 + 13 = 18  |  5 + 5 + 8 = 18   ← level
   *   three columns: 5 | 13 + 5 | 5 + 8               ← a short first column
   *                                                     with a hole under it
   *
   * Three columns was tried and is what the screenshot showed: `Obecně` alone
   * at the top left with half a column of nothing beneath it. Two columns also
   * gives each card enough width that a two-word entry does not wrap.
   *
   * The fix is NOT to reorder the groups so they pack better. Their order is
   * the old site's and this pass does not reorder content.
   */
  .prehled-grid {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    /* The measure still matters: a 1280-wide two-column list of two-word
       entries is mostly whitespace with a tick at each end. */
    max-width: 62rem;
    columns: 1;
    column-gap: 2rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .prehled-grid {
      columns: 2;
      column-gap: 2.5rem;
    }
  }

  /*
   * --color-kamen fill, not --color-omitka: the section itself is --omitka now
   * (see the file header), so a white card on a white ground would have shown
   * only a hairline for an edge. Stone-on-white reads as a card without one.
   */
  .skupina {
    break-inside: avoid;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    background-color: var(--color-kamen);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .skupina-nadpis {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    /* Public Sans, not Fraunces: this is a UI label at 16px and the display
       face is never used below 20px (docs/02-design-system.md §2.6). */
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-les);
  }

  .skupina-ikona {
    flex: none;
    /* An icon is a fill, so plain brass is correct here. */
    color: var(--color-mosaz);
  }

  .skupina ul {
    margin: 0.875rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .skupina li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }

  .skupina li + li {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .polozka-ikona {
    flex: none;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--color-mosaz);
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  /* The one entry with a caveat is marked differently, not just worded so. */
  .polozka-ikona--overit {
    color: var(--color-mosaz-tmava);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .polozka-overit {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
    font-size: var(--text-caption);
    color: var(--color-kura);
  }
</style>
